# PATENT CLAIM

**Claim 1:**

An ultrasonic probe device for inspecting welding defects on cylindrical nuclear reactor vessel penetrations, comprising:

a control head having a curvilinear body configured to conform to an outer cylindrical surface of a reactor vessel penetration, said control head defining:

(a) a concave contact surface having a radius of curvature substantially matching an outer diameter of the cylindrical penetration to be inspected, said concave contact surface extending circumferentially through an arc of between 90 and 180 degrees and axially along a length sufficient to span a heat-affected zone adjacent a circumferential weld joint;

(b) at least one ultrasonic transducer housing disposed within said control head, said housing defining a transducer cavity oriented at a predetermined incidence angle relative to a normal of said concave contact surface, said incidence angle being selected within a range of 30 to 70 degrees to generate a refracted shear wave suitable for detection of volumetric and planar discontinuities within the weld joint and heat-affected zone;

(c) a coupling channel formed within said control head and fluidly connected to said concave contact surface, said coupling channel configured to deliver an acoustic couplant between said concave contact surface and the outer cylindrical surface of the penetration during inspection;

(d) a guide track disposed along a peripheral edge of said control head, said guide track configured to engage a corresponding rail or fixture affixed proximate the penetration, thereby constraining movement of said control head to a helical or circumferential scanning path along the weld joint;

a transducer assembly received within said transducer cavity, said transducer assembly comprising a piezoelectric element electrically coupled to a signal cable extending through a strain-relief conduit integrally formed within said control head;

a position-encoding mechanism operatively coupled to said guide track, said position-encoding mechanism configured to generate positional data correlated with an angular or axial position of said control head relative to the weld joint; and

a housing enclosure surrounding said control head, said housing enclosure comprising a wear-resistant contact layer disposed at said concave contact surface and configured to minimize friction during scanning movement of said control head along the outer cylindrical surface of the penetration;

wherein said control head is dimensioned and shaped to maintain substantially continuous acoustic coupling with the outer cylindrical surface of the penetration throughout a scanning operation, thereby enabling detection of welding defects including but not limited to lack of fusion, incomplete penetration, porosity, and cracking within the weld joint and adjacent heat-affected zone.

---

**Claim 2 (dependent):**

The ultrasonic probe device of claim 1, wherein said concave contact surface further comprises a plurality of discrete segments, each segment having a radius of curvature independently adjustable to accommodate penetrations of varying outer diameters within a range of 50 mm to 300 mm.

**Claim 3 (dependent):**

The ultrasonic probe device of claim 1, wherein said transducer housing comprises a plurality of transducer cavities arranged in an array along the axial length of said control head, each cavity oriented at a distinct incidence angle selected from the range of 30 to 70 degrees, thereby enabling simultaneous or sequential generation of multiple refracted shear wave modes for comprehensive defect characterization.

**Claim 4 (dependent):**

The ultrasonic probe device of claim 1, further comprising a temperature-compensation element disposed within said control head, said temperature-compensation element configured to adjust an acoustic velocity correction factor based on a sensed temperature of the outer cylindrical surface of the penetration during inspection at elevated operating temperatures characteristic of nuclear reactor service conditions.
